From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:31:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: allwinner: a733-dp: Allow
 #sound-dai-cells

The transmitter has an audio half, fed by the I2S3 controller over an
internal connection (user manual sections 17.1.1 and 15.4.7.66). The
driver registers an HDMI codec under the transmitter's device, and a
sound card names that codec with the phandle of the node, so the node is
a sound DAI with a single DAI and no cell.

Allow #sound-dai-cells = <0> and take the common DAI properties, which
turns additionalProperties into unevaluatedProperties.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: the sound card binds to the transmitter; audio
not heard, no DisplayPort sink with speakers was at hand.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/display/allwinner,sun60i-a733-dp.yaml       | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/allwinner,sun60i-a733-dp.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/allwinner,sun60i-a733-dp.yaml
index 7983157ab8df..12639ff0ec7b 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/allwinner,sun60i-a733-dp.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/allwinner,sun60i-a733-dp.yaml
@@ -15,6 +15,9 @@ description: |
   TCON TV1, sends the main link through the first combo PHY of the SERDES
   block and the AUX channel through the AUX PHY beside it.
 
+allOf:
+  - $ref: /schemas/sound/dai-common.yaml#
+
 properties:
   compatible:
     const: allwinner,sun60i-a733-dp
@@ -56,6 +59,9 @@ properties:
   power-domains:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  "#sound-dai-cells":
+    const: 0
+
   ports:
     $ref: /schemas/graph.yaml#/properties/ports
 
@@ -86,7 +92,7 @@ required:
   - phy-names
   - ports
 
-additionalProperties: false
+unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
@@ -106,6 +112,7 @@ examples:
         resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_EDP>;
         phys = <&dp_aux_phy>, <&combophy0 PHY_TYPE_DP>;
         phy-names = "aux", "dp";
+        #sound-dai-cells = <0>;
 
         ports {
             #address-cells = <1>;
